**Begin the shared area core:** [Begin with substances, particles and chemical accounting](core/Substances-particles-and-chemical-accounting.lingua#r_06A721F480CCA6DC7EB5D006D8).

The area core is being developed across Hephaestus before further specialist extensions. Existing deeper trails remain available for reference; completing one does not complete this broader area.

Understand substances, structure, transformations, and the evidence supporting chemical claims. [General chemistry](general-chemistry/General-chemistry.lingua#r_206GS6CVXD8WSY1VX7PRF7136V) begins from ordinary materials and chemical language, then develops quantitative reactions, electronic structure, bonding, phases, energy, rates, equilibria, electrochemistry, chemical measurement, laboratory work, and independent research.

Reuse [Inquiry — shared ways to understand and investigate](../inquiry/Inquiry.lingua#r_75MNKZQKNB0XBG021SWWW2HASB) and connect the question with [Ergon — useful labor and productive knowledge](../../Ergon.lingua#r_FE78A5A2D2A3261F711703DCC1), [Hephaestus](../Hephaestus.lingua#r_00000000000000000000002001), and [Philosophy](../../../scholazein/philosophy/Philosophy.lingua#r_00000000000000000000001001). Follow the particular chemical problem into its related material, biological, environmental, and production questions.

[Mineralogy and petrology — minerals, crystals, rock processes, and investigation](../../gaia/earth/mineralogy-and-petrology/Mineralogy-and-petrology.lingua#r_44F7X6GPMW6ZSCCN6D71QSVKBN) connects crystal chemistry and phase models with measured mineral properties and rock histories. Follow its analytical and phase studies for mineral/rock questions, keeping the shared [General chemistry](general-chemistry/General-chemistry.lingua#r_206GS6CVXD8WSY1VX7PRF7136V) foundations available.

Follow chemical transformations from variable feed through specified products, industrial processes, operation and recovery in [Industrial chemistry — chemical transformations, useful products and continuing production](industrial-chemistry/Industrial-chemistry.lingua#r_3AKBAFB2ABJ0671QW6ZBQ0B618).

Connect manufactured substances with the quality, transfer and continuing supply systems delivering them through [Chemical feedstocks and supply systems — specified materials from origin to accepted use](../materials/chemical-feedstocks-and-supply-systems/Chemical-feedstocks-and-supply-systems.lingua#r_05V6FYWMN0VND552CQE94HHA2Q).

**Developed first common foundation:** material questions, substances and phases, observations and symbols, formulas, atomic evidence and isotopes, quantities, uncertainty boundaries, conservation, reaction extent and limiting amounts. Twelve existing lessons supply the shared formation; three new Records connect the quantity preparation, integrated study and review. Follow the core continuation from the opening above. The study distinguishes component transfer from reaction and an allowed composition from an experimentally established one. Bonding, energy, phases, rates, equilibrium and analytical evidence remain part of the later common formation.

**Developed second common foundation:** spectral quantities, electronic-state models and configurations, periodic comparisons, valence/formal-charge accounts, geometry/polarity, interactions, thermal boundaries, calorimetry and phase descriptions. Six new lessons reuse ten general-chemistry Records in a sixteen-step continuation after the first review. A study distinguishes spectral and structural representations from an invented phase-energy model, with independent exact checks. Full quantum, thermodynamic, kinetic, equilibrium and analytical formation remains unfinished. Continue comparable computing work next.

