The new lessons distinguish oxidation state, Lewis formal charge and actual species charge; derive acidic and formal basic half-reaction balances with independent atom/charge checks; connect reaction normalization, extent and electron amount; and separate external electron flow, chemical transfer, ionic transport and paired interfacial charge storage. BIPM's exact defining e and N_A give F=96485.3321233100184 C mol⁻¹. Positive F is distinguished from negative electron charge, and the investigation's positive reduction-oriented current magnitude is explicitly translated to the Green Book's negative cathodic-current convention. Exact constants do not make physical measurements exact.

The original hypothetical aggregate ledger uses Cu²⁺+Zn→Cu+Zn²⁺ and Fe³⁺+½Zn→Fe²⁺+½Zn²⁺. In reference amount n*=1 μmol and species order (Cu²⁺,Cu,Fe³⁺,Fe²⁺,Zn,Zn²⁺,X⁻), initial amounts (3,0,4,0,5,0,18) conserve Cu=3, Fe=4, Zn=5 and net chemical charge zero. X⁻ is an unchanged monovalent spectator species, not an invented element. With x=1,y=3/2, the final amounts are (2,1,5/2,3/2,13/4,7/4,18). Chemical electron-equivalent H=2x+y=7/2, stored equivalent s=1/2 and external N=4 close both electrode accounts, with paired surface-charge changes ±Fs n*. Internal ionic transport, spatial charge density and interface constitutive behavior remain unspecified.

For τ=t/(100 s) on [0,2], the prescribed rates are x′=(1+τ)/4, y′=3(1+τ)/8 and s′=(1+τ)/8. Their integrated forms in g=τ+τ²/2 prove nonnegative reactant stocks throughout the interval. The stipulated current is I_e=(F n*/100 s)(1+τ) and terminal voltage is V=(1−τ/4) V, with V=V_cathode−V_anode and positive V I_e delivering electrical power. Work is 17/6 in units E*=F n*×1 V; multiplying separate time means instead gives 3. Charge-weighted mean voltage is 17/24 V. A separately supplied whole-assembly ΔU=−4E*, with no other work, implies Q_in=−7E*/6. Terminal data alone do not establish chemical free energy, interface energy, heat or efficiency. Entropy, chemical potential and reversible-work/voltage derivation remain required subsequent common preparation.

Recovery r=3/4 gives collected copper c=3/4 and uncollected copper 1/4. Copper/iron/storage fractions of external charge are 1/2,3/8,1/8; copper's Faradaic fraction is 4/7, collected-copper equivalent is 3/8 and Cu²⁺ conversion is 1/3. Purity and energy efficiency require separate quantities. Given only N=4,s=1/2,c=3/4 and the stocks, the full feasible family is x∈[3/4,7/4], y=7/2−2x, r=3/(4x). Independent y=3/2 identifies x=1,r=3/4. These are ledger-compatible alternatives, not claimed physically realized devices with identical voltage traces. Opposing signed partial currents demonstrate why a general reaction/net-current ratio need not lie in [0,1]; zero denominators remain undefined.

