The sixth chemistry block is installed after `@chemistry-electron-review`. Nine new lessons and three preserved shared Records form the exact continuation: `chemistry-thermo-constraints`, `th-potentials`, `chemistry-mixture-potential`, `chemistry-ideal-mixture`, `chemistry-reaction-derivative`, `gc-gibbs`, `chemistry-equilibrium-minimum`, `gc-chemical-potential`, `chemistry-reversible-cell`, `chemistry-thermo-evidence`, `chemistry-free-energy-study`, `chemistry-free-energy-review`. Chemistry now has **85 common learning Records**. The thermal-potential, Gibbs and chemical-potential Records retain original prose, identities, imports and specialist continuations, with bounded common-reading notes appended. Existing entropy, solution/quotient, cell, mathematical differential and investigative Records remain contextual reuse; no competing continuation was added to an already selected Record.

The closed-system comparison declares a heat reservoir T₀, pressure-volume work p₀ΔV, non-pressure-volume work W′ positive out, equilibrium endpoints at matching T₀,p₀ and no omitted net storage/exchange. It derives ΔG+W′=−T₀S_gen and W′≤−ΔG. The fixed-volume counterpart uses Helmholtz A=U−TS. A hypothetical ΔU=−100 J,ΔV=0.001 m³,p₀=100 kPa,ΔS=0.5 J/K,T₀=300 K gives ΔG=−150 J; W′=200 J closes energy but gives −1/6 J/K generation. The state-model extension dU=T dS−p dV+Σμ_i dn_i is explicitly a physical premise. Product-rule differentials, constrained partial derivatives, homogeneous scaling G=Σn_iμ_i and fixed-T,p Gibbs–Duhem are derived with their domain qualifications.

The ideal neutral-gas mixture is derived through a reversible reference mixing account, with Δ_mixS=−RΣn_i ln x_i and zero ideal enthalpy of mixing. At fixed T, pure-gas pressure integration and mixing give G=Σn_iμ_i°+RT[Σn_i ln(n_i/N)+N ln(p/p°)] and μ_i=μ_i°+RT ln(x_i p/p°). Activity is distinguished from this constitutive expression. Changing a reference by a_i′=c_i a_i requires μ_i°′=μ_i°−RT ln c_i. Species labels must represent physically distinct constituents; no statistical foundation or real mixture validation is claimed.

Reaction extent n_i=n_i,0+ν_iξ and the chain rule give Δ_rG=dG/dξ=Σν_iμ_i, distinct from finite ΔG=∫Δ_rG dξ. Dimensionless Q=∏a_i^ν_i yields Δ_rG=Δ_rG°+RT lnQ and the allowed interior equilibrium condition Q=K. Reaction rescaling, reversal, pressure factors and reference transformations are explicit. A⇌B conserves total amount and cancels ideal pressure factors; A⇌2B generally does neither. Boundary/constraint and stability qualifications prevent a stationary sign rule from being mistaken for a global equilibrium proof.

The original ideal A⇌B model at p=p° uses y=n_B/N, μ_A°=0,μ_B°=−RT lnK and G=NRTφ(y), with φ=y ln(y/K)+(1−y)ln(1−y). Its derivative ln[y/(K(1−y))] and positive second derivative 1/[y(1−y)] prove the unique global minimum y*=K/(1+K), including continuous endpoint limits x ln x→0. The minimum is −NRT ln(1+K). For N=5 mol,K=4,T=300 K,y:1/2→4/5, Δξ=3/2 mol and ΔG=−5RT ln(5/4); available work is **2782.978073825934… J**. Initial derivative times Δξ is different from this finite change. Starting at y=8/9 gives Q=8 and a positive reaction derivative, favoring the reverse direction. Stipulated K at each temperature does not define a real material's K(T).

A separately declared reversible whole-cell work model gives Δ_rG=−zF E_rev with z dimensionless and transferred amount zξ. Reaction normalization preserves E_rev; finite work needs the varying-potential integral. The neutral A/B model is not claimed to be a cell. Current, junction effects, polarization, activity conventions and interfacial storage remain distinct from a reversible potential. An optional kinetic model requires k_f/k_r=K for consistency; then dG/dt≤0 follows from the sign of the logarithm. Equal forward/reverse rates with K=4 at y=3/5 give the explicit incompatible undriven-direction counterexample. Thermodynamic equilibrium evidence is separated from observed stationarity and rate fitting.

The original `free_energy_study.py` and `free_energy_checks.py` reuse unchanged `reaction_study.py`, `entropy_checks.py` and its dependency `entropy_study.py`. Installed extraction passed **10,773 checks** through Nix/Python 3.14.8: **756 binary cases, 54 general mixtures, 15 finite-change integrals, 54 quotient transformations, 36 reversible-cell cases and 54 work/entropy screens**, plus source calculations, defining-constant products and invalid inputs. Decimal precision is 70 digits; rational logarithm enclosures have the earlier proved remainder. Independent midpoint integration uses 16/64 panels and the proved error bound M(b−a)³/(24m²), M=1/a²+1/(1−b)² for the reaction-derivative integrand on interior intervals. The additional 10⁻⁶⁰ comparison tolerance describes arithmetic rounding, not physical uncertainty. Exact proofs establish continuous claims; finite cases verify implementations.

